FIX (CRITICAL): Gate the sessionShownRef flip in BOTH /app/frontend/app/chat/[id].tsx and /app/frontend/app/(tabs)/chat.tsx so it only flips to true AFTER settings have actually loaded. The simplest fix is to read `wpSettings.settings` (already exposed by ChatSettingsProvider) and require it to be non-null before short-circuiting the gate. Example for chat/[id].tsx around line 216-236: replace with:
```
const settingsLoaded = wpSettings.settings !== null;
const locked = wpSettings.isThreadLocked(threadId);
const alreadyUnlocked = sessionShownRef.current || wpSettings.isUnlocked(threadId);
if (settingsLoaded && locked && !alreadyUnlocked) {
  return (<SafeAreaView ...><ChatLockGate ... /></SafeAreaView>);
}
if (settingsLoaded && !locked) {
  sessionShownRef.current = true; // only flip AFTER we KNOW chat is unlocked
}
if (!settingsLoaded) {
  return (<SafeAreaView ...><ActivityIndicator /></SafeAreaView>); // brief loading state
}
```
Same change in (tabs)/chat.tsx ChatTabGate. The key invariant: sessionShownRef must only flip to true after we have CONFIRMED (via real settings, not null) that the chat is currently unlocked. Then the original iter22 logic correctly prevents the bounce when lock flips mid-session.
